Kept so `console/public` exists in git and therefore in the Docker build context.

console/Dockerfile does `COPY --from=build /app/public ./public`, and an empty
directory is not tracked by git - so without this file the build fails on a clean
checkout with "/app/public: not found", which is exactly how it failed once.

Dropping the COPY instead would make the build pass and silently omit the first asset
anybody puts here.
